eai-robowits - contents, licenses, and the BlenderKit models it leaves out

The image (images/robowits/Dockerfile) contains:
  - RoboWits @ 9cc30ae (github.com/UMass-Embodied-AGI/RoboWits): MIT, as declared in its pyproject.toml (the repository
    ships no LICENSE file);
  - Genesis 0.4.7 and the rest of RoboWits' locked Python stack, each under its own license (Genesis: Apache-2.0);
  - RoboWits' HuggingFace asset bundle XHRlyb2001/RoboWits_assets (Apache-2.0): the robot and part of the task models
    (dominos, stand_pages and stack_cubes need nothing else);
  - the nvidia/cuda:12.9.1-base-ubuntu22.04 base (NVIDIA Deep Learning Container License, /NGC-DL-CONTAINER-LICENSE).

It does NOT contain the 127 BlenderKit models of RoboWits' seed tasks, which every RoboWits family except dominos,
stand_pages and stack_cubes loads. As of 2026-09-28, 118 are under BlenderKit's Royalty Free license and 9 under CC0;
62 need a Full Plan subscription.
BlenderKit (now Blendkit) licenses each model to the account that downloads it; its Terms (Art. 5.4, 5.8) forbid
distributing Royalty Free models apart from a project or in a form from which they can be opened or separated. So the
image, this repository and our published results never carry the model files in usable form; replay videos are
renders. The only copy we distribute is an ENCRYPTED bundle for research use, behind a click-through agreement (1b).

To run those families:
  1a. Fetch the models with your own BlenderKit API key: put BLENDERKIT_API_KEY=<key> into ../.env (next to the repo)
     and run `images/robowits/fetch_blenderkit.sh <dir>`.
     - It follows RoboWits' own recipe: assets/download_blenderkit_asset.py and the Blender conversion.
     - It adds two fixes our tasks need (blenderkit/Dockerfile):
       - pinch_card's retired "bank card" model is replaced by the "Apple Card" model, scaled;
       - two 16667-pixel textures are downscaled so that PIL loads them.
     - It checks every file against blenderkit.sha256, the files our instances were frozen with. A model changed
       upstream since then may not rebuild a frozen scene exactly: the verifier then reports instance_exact = 0.
  1b. Or use our encrypted bundle, the same files as blenderkit.sha256 lists, Fernet-encrypted: request access at
     https://huggingface.co/datasets/eai-v2-internal/robowits-blenderkit-encrypted (log in and accept its research
     terms), run `hf auth login`, then `images/robowits/fetch_blenderkit_encrypted.sh <dir>` (it checks every file
     against blenderkit_encrypted.sha256).
     - The tooling (rcb_robowits.py) sees the key in the folder and decrypts only the models the task's family loads,
       at scene build, into a private tmpfs directory that it deletes as soon as the scene is built.
     - Terms: non-commercial academic research only, through this tooling only; no other decryption, extraction or
       conversion; no sharing or re-upload of the files or the key; models stay their authors' (ATTRIBUTION.csv).
     - What it does not do: a privileged-mode agent is root in its container, where the folder and its key are
       mounted, so it could decrypt the models itself. The encryption keeps the models from being copied around
       as ordinary files; it does not hide them from a process inside the task container.
  2. `export RCB_ROBOWITS_BLENDERKIT=<dir>`. Each of those tasks mounts it read-only at /opt/robowits/assets/blender_kit
     (environment/ and tests/ docker-compose.yaml; the sim sidecar in the standard twins).
Keep the folder private.
